## 1. Firmware platform and ESP-IDF components

Building the firmware requires [ESP-IDF](https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf)
and pulls in many Espressif and upstream libraries transitively (FreeRTOS,
lwIP, mbedTLS, NimBLE, drivers, etc.).

| Component | Source | License |
|-----------|--------|---------|
| ESP-IDF | https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf | Apache-2.0 |
| LVGL | https://github.com/lvgl/lvgl (via `main/idf_component.yml`, ^9.2.2) | MIT |
| esp_websocket_client | https://github.com/espressif/esp-protocols (component registry) | Apache-2.0 |

LVGL may bundle fonts such as **Montserrat** under the
[SIL Open Font License 1.1](https://scripts.sil.org/OFL).

**Note:** A full ESP-IDF build produces a larger dependency tree than this
list. For compliance when shipping firmware images, refer to Espressif’s
licensing guidance and the `COPYING` / `LICENSE` files inside your installed
ESP-IDF tree and `managed_components/`.

