### 4.2 CJK font binary

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| Character lists | `third_party/fonts/tyz_7000_chars.txt`, `extra_symbols.txt` |
| Build-time TTF | **SimHei** (`simhei.ttf`), typically `C:\Windows\Fonts\simhei.ttf` on Windows — **not committed to this repo** |
| Generated output | `firmware/data/font_cjk_16.bin`, flashed to `cjk_font` partition |
| Tool | [lv_font_conv](https://github.com/lvgl/lv_font_conv) (MIT) via `scripts/gen_cjk_font.py` |

**SimHei / 黑体 is a proprietary font.** This project uses it only on the
build machine to rasterize glyphs into a binary font for the device. **You are
responsible for ensuring you have the right to use SimHei (or substitute another
licensed TTF) when generating and redistributing `font_cjk_16.bin`.** The MIT
license on this repository does not grant font embedding rights.

The 7000-character table follows the PRC *通用规范汉字表*; the list file itself
does not substitute for font licensing.

### 4.3 LVGL / UI fonts on device

- Status icons may use Montserrat (via LVGL, OFL).
- CJK UI text uses the generated binfont loaded from flash.

